p.src:
For the nonrelativistic dispersion relation, including the arbitrary offset, $\omega(k)=\frac{k^2}{2m}+C,$ the group velocity is $v_{\mathrm{group}}
=\frac{d}{dk}\left(\frac{k^2}{2m}+C\right)
=\frac{2k}{2m}
=\frac{k}{m}.$ The additive constant has disappeared, and the result is precisely the classical particle velocity.

